---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal title="Refund policy" description="If a guide is not what its page said it was, you get your money back. One email, no form.">
  <p>Short version: if a guide is not what its page said it was, you get your money back. One email, no form.</p>

  <h2>The legal position</h2>
  <p>A guide is digital content delivered by download. Before payment we ask for your express consent to immediate supply and acknowledgement that the fourteen-day right of withdrawal is lost when supply begins. This exception applies only when valid consent and confirmation have been provided. Your statutory rights for faulty, undelivered or misdescribed content are not limited by this policy or by the additional fourteen-day promise below.</p>

  <h2>What I do anyway</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Not as described.</strong> If the guide does not cover what its page and table of contents promised, write within fourteen days of purchase and it is refunded in full.</li>
    <li><strong>Bought twice.</strong> Duplicate purchases are refunded as soon as I see them, whether or not you write.</li>
    <li><strong>Download never worked.</strong> First I fix the link. If it cannot be fixed within two working days, you are refunded.</li>
    <li><strong>Changed your mind.</strong> If you have not downloaded the file, write within fourteen days and it is refunded without questions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is not refunded</h2>
  <p>Where the withdrawal exception validly applies, a change of mind after delivery is not covered by our additional promise. This does not exclude any refund or remedy required by law. The "who it is not for" section on every guide page exists so that this happens rarely.</p>

  <h2>How</h2>
  <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> from the address you paid with. Refunds go back to the original payment method through Stripe, usually within five to ten working days depending on your bank.</p>
</Legal>
